36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that sitting close together really helps us learn from one another. New joiners learned the unwritten rules by overhearing us, and project work became much faster when people were within earshot.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings show a disparity in the layout; the current plan leaves some without window access, which was a major complaint. Also, unplanned shuffles in the past have caused significant disruptions for weeks.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that we're billed for the floor area, not by person, so empty desks still cost us about 41,000 yen a month. Also, re-running power and network costs 6,200 yen per desk every time we change.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"That's a lot of money! As for my part, I found out that setting up at a new desk takes four to nine minutes every morning. Also, our arrival times vary wildly, from before 8:00 to after 10:00!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the physical reality is quite stubborn. There's a significant noise difference between the window and the door, and more importantly, the physio noted that getting a workstation ergonomically correct takes days of fine-tuning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have a difficult balance to strike. While being close helps us grow and work faster, we must also consider the physical comfort and the costs Daisuke mentioned.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The window access issue is particularly concerning. If we simply follow the plan, some will be disadvantaged. We must decide if we are willing to accept that inequality or find a way to rotate it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... @Toshio, if we rotate, wouldn't that mean we have to pay that 6,200 yen per desk fee more often? I'm worried that changing things too much will just keep costing us more money.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Wait, if we rotate, does that mean we'd be spending those four to nine minutes every single morning? And if we arrive at different times, wouldn't the early birds just take all the best spots?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. If we go for a free-for-all, the early arrivals claim the quiet window spots, and the rest of us suffer. Plus, the physio's note makes it clear that constant moving is a nightmare for our bodies.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It sounds like we are all very concerned about the downsides of moving too often. However, we cannot ignore how much we benefit from the natural conversations that happen when we sit together.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we prioritize stability to avoid costs and physical strain, we risk cementing an unfair distribution of the ""better"" seats. We must decide if we value consistency over equity.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want anyone to feel it's unfair, but the budget is so tight. If we keep changing the layout, the costs will just keep adding up. Maybe there's a way to be fair without moving too much?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,I agree with Daisuke! We can't just keep spending money or wasting time every morning. But @Toshio is right about the window seats. Is there a way to be fair without moving every single day?,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we want to avoid the daily chaos Mio mentioned and the physical strain I found, a free-address system is out. We need a solution that balances stability with a fair distribution of the environment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we are all leaning away from daily changes. Perhaps a system where we stay put for a while, but eventually move, would allow us to keep our connections while sharing the window light.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"A rotating system would address the inequality of the window seats and the complaints from the survey, while avoiding the daily instability and arrival-time bias that a free-address system would create.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I suppose that could work. As long as we don't move too often, the costs might be manageable. But we should still be very careful about how many times we shift.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm okay with that! As long as we aren't scrambling every morning, I can handle a move every now and then. It sounds like a good middle ground for everyone!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a compromise, I suppose. It avoids the daily ergonomic nightmare and the ""first-come, first-served"" lottery, while ensuring no one is permanently stuck in the noise by the door. Let's see the options.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
